# RAC (frpc) reverse-tunnel config TEMPLATE — station WITHOUT a hypervisor.
# sigmond-rac/install.sh renders this to /etc/sigmond/frpc.toml.template with
# this station's identity filled in.  To ACTIVATE, get this station's remote
# port assignment from the WsprDaemon admin (Rob), fill the <...> values, then:
#   sudo cp /etc/sigmond/frpc.toml.template /etc/sigmond/frpc.toml
#   sudo systemctl restart wd-rac
#
# ON A DASI2 SITE, DO NOT ARM THIS ONE.  There the site's single login lives
# on the Proxmox host (frpc-host.toml, installed by install-host.sh) and
# forwards the VM's ports across the bridge, so the VM needs no tunnel of
# its own.  The gateway files one key per login id, so arming both would get
# whichever connects second refused — the guard, not a bug.  This template
# is for a sigmond station that runs on bare metal with no hypervisor
# beneath it.
#
# Gateway: sigmond stations tunnel to HamSCI's own server, vpn.hamsci.org,
# not to WsprDaemon's gw2.  :35736 is its frps-secure instance (TLS forced,
# trust-on-first-use auth); :35735 is the legacy open frps that the older
# HamSCI volunteer stations still use.  There is no registrar here.
#
# Identity: the gateway's TOFU plugin admits a login that carries a user id
# and a pubkey in [metadatas].  The FIRST login to claim a given user id
# files its pubkey; later logins must present the same key, so nothing else
# can take this station's identity.  The token is NOT the gate and is empty
# by design.  Re-keying a station means the admin must first delete its
# entry from the gateway registry, or the new key is refused.
#
# This tunnel carries what the STATION serves: sshd (vm-ssh), ka9q-web
# (vm-web), and any further service it grows.
#
# Services and ports: a station has ONE number (its RAC/DASI number), and
# each service it publishes gets a band whose remote port is a fleet-wide
# base plus that number — vm-ssh 35800+n, vm-web 45800+n, and so on.  The
# band table and the list of what this station publishes live in
# config/rac-bands.sh and SIGMOND_RAC_PROXIES.  Admins reach every port at
# the gateway's VPN address, 10.3.2.1:<port>.
# Proxy names are "<reporter ID>-<band>"; the rac-dashboard keys on those
# band suffixes to group a station's tunnels, so do not rename them.


# The [[proxies]] blocks are appended here by the installer, one per
# service in this site's proxy set — see config/rac-bands.sh.
